  "implemented": [
    "Windows ConPTY with real console input/output and resize; process created suspended, assigned to an unnamed kill-on-close Job Object, then resumed.",
    "Windows PowerShell command syntax is advertised; startup profiles are disabled. Unsupported ConPTY exports withhold the capability instead of substituting redirected pipes.",
    "Bounded cleanup reports uncertainty and retains workspace reservations when owned process cleanup cannot be confirmed, including failed post-launch setup.",
    "Retired-child history removal rechecks ownership under the handoff/input lock.",
    "Native Windows tests cover actual console APIs, Unicode, resize, partial input, exact descendant-handle termination, denied startup, takeover, retry/conflict fences, parent handoff, cleanup/reservation release and Ctrl-C. Test executables cross-compile; native execution is pending.",
    "Installed Windows acceptance now composes real backend/frontend children, correlated schema messages, a real HTTP integration in ConPTY, server transfer and human keyboard takeover/return/end through the emulator. Shared scenario passed on the macOS development app using POSIX PTY; this is not Windows evidence."
  ],
